  "id": "Compound::DB00511 - Gene::486",
  "verbalization": "Acetyldigitoxin appears to interact with Atp1b3 and Atp1a3, both of which are involved in sodium-potassium ATPase activity, a critical process in maintaining cellular ion homeostasis. This interaction is reflected in the evidence that Acetyldigitoxin binds to these proteins, which in turn are involved in the activity of Fxyd2. The shared involvement of Atp1b3 and Atp1a3 in sodium-potassium ATPase activity suggests a potential mechanism by which Acetyldigitoxin influences Fxyd2, possibly through modulation of ion transport processes. The consistent presence of Fxyd2 as a participant in these activities, across multiple paths, indicates a possible functional link between Acetyldigitoxin and Fxyd2, likely mediated through the regulation of ion transport activity. The evidence supports a role for Acetyldigitoxin in modulating the function of Fxyd2, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
